Package: glscalibrator
Type: Package
Title: Automated Calibration and End-to-End Analysis of GLS (Global Location Sensor) Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Fabio", "Favoretto", email = "favoretto.fabio@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6493-4254")),
    person("Cecilia", "Soldatini", email = "csoldatini@cicese.mx",
           role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8112-3162")))
Maintainer: Fabio Favoretto <favoretto.fabio@gmail.com>
Description: Provides a fully automated, end-to-end workflow for light-level
    geolocation (GLS) data from seabirds and other wildlife. In addition to the
    threshold calibration workflow (twilight detection, automatic calibration
    period detection, batch position estimation) the package now wraps a
    complete movement-model pipeline: it reads raw logger light, temperature and
    wet/dry channels, deduces in-situ sea-surface temperature, acquires
    environmental fields (NOAA OI SST and a land mask), and reconstructs
    most-probable tracks with credible intervals using a particle model
    (probGLS). The pipeline is configuration-driven and taxon-agnostic: all
    biology (movement speeds, colony, tolerances) lives in a validated
    'probgls_config' object, so it applies to any GLS deployment, not a
    particular species. Implements the established threshold workflow internally,
    following the methods described in SGAT, GeoLight and TwGeos, and the
    particle algorithm of Merkel et al. (2016) <doi:10.1186/s40462-016-0072-y>.
